Fair value before the reveal is 13 (die 1 mean 9.25 + die 2 mean 3.75), with possible sums 7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 18, 19. The history so far points to a middling-to-high informed share (roughly 0.5 on average), so quoting inside the 8–18 range loses more to informed traders than it earns from noise traders.

At bid 8 / ask 18, an informed trader only trades when the sum is 7 or 19, and then I lose just 1. Those extremes are also less likely now, given no trade at the same quotes last time. Noise traders who hit these prices give me about 5 of edge each. Nearby prices (17.5, 18.3, 19) come out slightly worse on my estimate, so I am keeping the same quote.

