Fair value before the reveal is 13, and the distribution is symmetric about it (7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 18, 19). The history points to alpha of about 0.5: two trades were clearly noise, but an informed buyer likely hit the 16.2 ask in round 1.

At that alpha, quoting exactly at 8 and 18 is the best spot. An informed trader only trades there when the value is 7 or 19, and loses me just 1 when it does, while a noise trade earns about 5 of edge. Tighter quotes lose more to informed traders at 18/19 and 7/8 than they gain from noise.

