Die 3 = 9, so the contract settles at 9 unless die 1 or die 2 shows 10, which happens with probability 1 − (5/6)(3/4) = 0.375. The value is therefore 9 (62.5%) or 10 (37.5%), with fair value 9.375.

Bidding 9 and asking 10 cannot lose: an informed counterparty never sells at 9 or buys at 10, since the value is never below 9 or above 10. Noise traders still trade on both sides, giving an edge of 0.375 on a buy and 0.625 on a sell. Tightening either side would expose me to informed traders, and the run of no-trades so far suggests alpha is probably high.

